bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, 0, "Measured (base seed aa542919a298e130 = origin f43f68c218e, release/1.0.0, aarch64, JIT): fn g(x, k: i64) -> i64 with a nil match, called 4e8 times as g(Col.Red, 0) + g(raw, 0). Adding a never-taken branch 'if k > 5: val t = h(k, 1, 2) + ... + h(k, 30, 2); return t' raises wall time 1.10s -> 1.95s (+2.1 ns per call); moving the same 30 calls into a separate fn slow(x, k) called from that branch is flat (1.10-1.16s). The cranelift function pays prologue/frame (callee-saved spills) for every call it contains on every entry, even when the branch never runs."
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, 1, "Repro: cold0.spl vs cold30.spl vs coldout.spl (30 h() calls inline in a dead branch vs outlined); alternate run order. Expected: a never-taken cold branch costs ~0 on the hot path (shrink-wrapping / cold-block outlining), so source does not have to outline by hand. Workaround in use: seed_jit_any_match_bare_none_arm_misses_user_enum_none_2026-11-27 moved its registration path into one __erased_none_arm_slow_* helper per module."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, P3, closed, "stale: FIXED by p3sweep4-20261127 (new cold-outline MIR pass: conditional cold arms with 8+ calls collapse to a synthetic helper; prologue spill stores eliminated); 24 percent entry overhead removed; spec 3/3 2026-11-27", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/codegen/common_backend.rs, 0, NONE, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_fix_claims |bug_id, state, session_id, claimed_at, heartbeat_at, prev_status, note|
    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T21:20:35Z, 2026-11-27T21:20:35Z, open, "wave10"

    seed_jit_never_taken_branch_calls_cost_frame_on_every_entry_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: measured 4e8 calls/run: cold30 +24-25 percent per-entry cost vs cold0 (5-6 vs 4 ns; disassembly showed sub rsp,0x120 + 7 callee-saved spill stores in every g30 entry). Root cause: compile_function_body lowers all MIR blocks into one Cranelift function; cranelift-codegen 0.116 has no shrink-wrapping, so regalloc2 callee-saved assignments and the full frame land in the prologue. Fix: NEW codegen/cold_outline.rs (wired after inlining, before referenced_call_names): a conditional-arm block (single predecessor, not on a cycle, >=8 call-like instrs by default, ends in return, portable instructions only) collapses to one call to a synthetic __cold_outline_* helper; live-in vregs + touched local slots become params (LocalAddr re-indexes cleanly); conservative guards (SSA escape checks, type agreement, <=32 params, no asm/bridge). Behavior unchanged by construction; taken-path outputs bit-identical; SIMPLE_COLD_OUTLINE_MIN_CALLS=0 escape hatch confirms the mechanism (ratio returns to ~1.20). Spec jit_cold_branch_frame_cost (SIMPLE_BINARY convention, ratio pin + lane receipt + taken-path pins) 3/3; 5 new unit tests; jit_reachability_prune + jit_parallel_translate pass; 5 example programs output-identical. Residuals: merge/fall-through and Switch arms stay inline (documented); a taken outlined arm pays one extra call (accepted tradeoff). close_evidence reproducer=test/05_perf/compiler/jit_cold_branch_frame_cost_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/jit_const_size_u8_repeat_literal_budget_spec.spl"
